Subject: [PATCH] cgroup: let CAP_SYS_NICE move tasks between v1 cgroups

Android's system_server (uid 1000, CAP_SYS_NICE) moves app threads
between the top-app, foreground and background cpusets. Mainline only
allows root or the task's own uid to do that, so every move failed with
"libprocessgroup: AddTidToCgroup failed ... Permission denied" and apps
kept the cpuset they were forked into. Android common kernels carry the
same CAP_SYS_NICE exemption.

--- a/kernel/cgroup/cgroup-v1.c
+++ b/kernel/cgroup/cgroup-v1.c
@@ -521,9 +521,16 @@
 	 */
 	cred = of->file->f_cred;
 	tcred = get_task_cred(task);
+	/*
+	 * Android: system_server (uid system, CAP_SYS_NICE) moves app threads
+	 * between the top-app, foreground and background cpusets. Android
+	 * common kernels allow that with CAP_SYS_NICE; without it every move
+	 * fails with EACCES and apps keep their cpuset from fork.
+	 */
 	if (!uid_eq(cred->euid, GLOBAL_ROOT_UID) &&
 	    !uid_eq(cred->euid, tcred->uid) &&
-	    !uid_eq(cred->euid, tcred->suid))
+	    !uid_eq(cred->euid, tcred->suid) &&
+	    !ns_capable(tcred->user_ns, CAP_SYS_NICE))
 		ret = -EACCES;
 	put_cred(tcred);
 	if (ret)
